Assesses one synthetic version of the Mayo PBC data (`survival::pbcseq`), made with the PART 1 generator.
Each section asks one question about the synthetic data, in this order:

1. Real data
2. Generate synthetic data
3. Visits and missing values: are the visit pattern and the gaps the same?
4. Patient traits: same mix of treatment / sex / age, without copying real patients?
5. Distributions: does each variable look the same on its own?
6. Correlations: do the labs move together the same way?
7. Trajectories: same change over time?
8. Within-patient structure: same patient-to-patient spread, slopes and visit-to-visit correlation?
9. Model transfer: does the PBC model give the same answer on synthetic data?
10. Overall utility and privacy
11. Summary


